I'd change the hero before touching anything else.
"We help businesses get customers, operate smarter and grow.

From advertising and websites to custom software and AI automation, Sales Cowboy helps businesses attract customers and build the systems to serve them."

8. What's missing from the website entirely?
These are the sections I'd prioritise.
A results-driven portfolio

Show at least three real projects. Ideally, one advertising campaign, one website or software project, and one automation or branding engagement.

Include before-and-after examples, actual deliverables and measurable results where available.


Testimonials and client logos

Use genuine client feedback with names and company names where permission is available. A testimonial describing a specific problem solved is more useful than “Excellent service.”


Who you serve

Your services are broad, but your audience is undefined. Feature the industries where you have the strongest experience: for example, real estate, retail, professional services, education or logistics, depending on your actual client base.

Visitors should recognise their own business in your website.


A clearer delivery process

“Talk, Build, Grow” is too vague. Explain discovery, proposal and scope, delivery milestones, approval, launch and ongoing support. Clients need to know what happens after they pay.


Service-specific pages

Someone searching for CRM automation should not land on a generic page dominated by web design and ads. Build dedicated pages around the services that have real commercial demand, with clear deliverables, FAQs, relevant examples and calls to action.


A proper qualification process

Ask what the visitor needs, their business type, budget range and desired timeline. Keep it short. A low-friction WhatsApp option should remain available for prospects who don't want to fill out a form.

9. The service descriptions need to sell outcomes, not activities
Several current descriptions are too vague to distinguish you from any other agency. Here are examples of stronger wording.
Current wording	Stronger positioning
“Meta, Google and TikTok campaigns.”	Paid campaigns designed to reach your target customers, generate qualified enquiries and track conversions.
“Workflows that follow up for you.”	CRM setup and automated follow-ups that help your team manage leads, reduce manual work and prevent missed enquiries.
“Rank higher. Get found locally.”	Local SEO and Google Business Profile optimisation to improve your visibility when nearby customers search for your services.
“Consistent, on-brand pages and daily reach.”	Social media management covering content planning, publishing, community engagement and performance reporting.
“Know your market before you spend.”	Competitor analysis, customer research and market insights to inform pricing, positioning and marketing decisions.
“24/7 care, security updates and fixes.”	Ongoing website maintenance, backups, security updates, monitoring and technical support, with a clearly defined service level.
“Register your business and stay compliant.”	CAC registration and clearly specified tax filing or compliance support, with the relevant professional qualifications and service limitations explained.

Don't promise increased revenue, rankings or leads as guaranteed outcomes. Sell the process, deliverables and measurement that give clients a credible route to those outcomes.

